      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T03:07:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m supporting my idea because of the following reasons:\n1) Most of the formula can\u0027t do the reverse, even for the well known E\u003dmc^2.\n   I don\u0027t think it would be a reason of not trusting it.\n   But yes good documentation is necessary to let people understand.\n2) IIRC, now you have a new set of unit tests that verify the behavior.\n   So I think it is feasible to prove the correctness.\n3) less code \u0026 less complexity usually means less maintain effort,\n   which I think is good for long term perspective.\n\nHowever, I do agree that this takes longer to evaluate.\nBut if you think this might be useful, then maybe a TODO somewhere is worthy in this commit?\n\nBesides, javadoc at one place provides the overall concept to users that haven\u0027t read through your code. And help they understand it if they need/don\u0027t need to read it.\nIn this case I think it is needed, while current in place comments don\u0027t give me enough context of how it is calculated.\nBut again, I\u0027m fine with it if other reviewers think it is ok.",
